{
  "Tabs and whole groups dragged as in a code editor: along a strip, to another group, beside a group or along an edge of the layout, between two managers, and the same moves from the keyboard. Every drop goes through the methods and events of what it does.": "",
  "Dragging tabs and groups": "",
  "A copy of the tab follows the pointer; a mark shows where it goes among tabs, and a translucent area which half of a group (or all of it) a drop would take. Resting on a tab of another group activates it; the strip scrolls near its ends. The content is moved, never made again.": "",
  "Dropped": "",
  "Reorders. A tab dropped among the pinned ones is pinned, one dropped among the others unpinned (`pinOnDrag`).": "",
  "Moves the tab there, at the place under the pointer; on the empty part of a strip, at the end.": "",
  "Moves the tab into that group, after its active tab (`openPosition`).": "",
  "Splits that group: a new group on that side with the tab. The edge zones are `dropEdgeSize` deep.": "",
  "A thin band along the manager's sides (`layoutEdgeSize`): a new group along that whole side (`layoutEdgeDrop`).": "",
  "Opens a copy there instead, when the document may be open twice (`allowDuplicate`, `copyModifier`).": "",
  "Moves the group with all its tabs beside another group or along an edge of the layout; into another group (or its strip) its tabs join that group.": "",
  "Floats in a window of its own (see [Dock and floating windows](/tabdocs/dock)); where it may not float (`allowFloat`), or over a manager outside its `dragGroup`, it is refused (`target: 'outside'`).": "",
  "Each part of drag and drop is a setting and changes live; a document's own `allowDrag` and a group's own `allowDrop` and `dropSides` win over the manager's.": "",
  "Between two managers": "",
  "Managers that share a `dragGroup` take each other's tabs and groups. The tab, its panel and its content go along; the other manager asks through its own `onOpening`, after `onMoving` in the first.": "",
  "Keys move the active tab along its strip or to another group, and “Move to…” (the tab's menu, the strip's menu for a whole group, Ctrl+K M, or `showMoveTo`) reaches every place a drag does, with the same areas shown and each place announced.": "",
  "Browser": "",
  "Installed app (desktop keys)": "",
  "Ctrl + Shift + Page Up / Page Down": "",
  "The active tab a place along its strip (`moveTabLeft`, `moveTabRight`).": "",
  "The active document to the next / previous group (`moveToNextGroup`, `moveToPreviousGroup`).": "",
  "To the group on that side, or into a new group there (`moveToGroupLeft`, `…Right`, `…Up`, `…Down`).": "",
  "\"Move to…\" for the active document (`moveTo`); the tab's menu and the strip's menu have it too.": "",
  "In “Move to…”": "",
  "A side of the group; again towards that side, the next group that way, or the edge of the layout; the other way, back to the middle (`targetLeft`, `targetRight`, `targetUp`, `targetDown`).": "",
  "The next / previous group, its middle (`targetNextGroup`, `targetPreviousGroup`).": "",
  "Moves it there (`targetDrop`).": "",
  "Leaves everything where it was (`targetCancel`); so does a press anywhere.": "",
  "Changing or refusing a drop": "",
  "`onDragOver` sees each place and may change it or refuse it; `onDropping` may still stop the drop. Then the events of what the drop does fire (`onMoved`, `onSplit`, …) and `onDropped`.": "",
  "\"Move to…\" reaches every place a pointer can: each side of each group, the edges of the layout, other managers of the same `dragGroup`.": "",
  "Each place \"Move to…\" points at is said (\"New group to the right of group 2\", or \"cannot go here\"), then moved, copied, split, or canceled.": "",
  "A long press starts the drag, so a swipe still scrolls the strip; held still and let go, it opens the tab's menu.": "",
  "Cancels a pointer drag too, and puts back what resting on tabs activated and what the strips scrolled.": "",
  "Tabs can be dragged; a document's own `allowDrag` wins.": "",
  "Groups can be dragged by the empty part of their bar.": "",
  "A handle at the start of each group's toolbar to drag the group by, also when its tabs fill the bar; a click on it (or Enter) starts “Move group to…”.": "",
  "Where a drop on a group's content may go; a group's own `dropSides` wins.": "",
  "How deep the edge zones of a group's content are: pixels, or a share.": "",
  "Drops along the edges of the whole layout, and how deep that band is, in pixels.": "",
  "How far, in pixels, the pointer moves before a press becomes a drag.": "",
  "How long, in milliseconds, a finger or a pen rests on a tab before it drags it; a swipe before that scrolls the strip.": "",
  "Resting on a tab of another group while dragging activates it, after that many milliseconds.": "",
  "Dragging across the border between pinned and other tabs pins or unpins; `false` keeps each tab on its side.": "",
  "The key that makes a drop a copy: Ctrl, Option on Apple platforms.": "",
  "Managers with the same name take each other's tabs and groups.": "",
  "The copy of the tab under the pointer; the strip scrolling near its ends.": "",
  "Drops into the group and beside it; `false` for a group that takes nothing. Saved with the layout.": "",
  "The group's own drop sides; `null` follows the manager. Saved with the layout.": "",
  "What a drop on a strip or into a group does (milestone 1).": "",
  "What a drop on an edge does; `null` splits the whole layout along that edge.": "",
  "A whole group beside `target` (`'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'`, `'down'`), into it (`'center'`), or along an edge of the layout (`target` `null`).": "",
  "A place along the strip (`-1` towards the start), not past the pinned or the other tabs.": "",
  "`'next'`, `'previous'`, or the group on that side (`'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'`, `'down'`); a new group when there is none.": "",
  "\"Move to…\" from the keyboard (see below).": "",
  "Stops a drag or \"Move to…\"; everything goes back.": "",
  "A target of your own, asked before the built-in one: `placeAt(x, y, drag)`, `marks(place, drag)`, `drop(place, drag)`. Returns the function that removes it.": "",
  "`{ document, group, manager, copy }` while something is dragged, else `null`.": "",
  "The targets in the order they are asked.": "",
  "`{ document, group, pointerType, byKeyboard }`, cancelable; `document` is `null` for a group.": "",
  "`{ document, from, target, manager, group, index, side, copy, byKeyboard }`: change the place, or `cancel` to refuse it. `target` is `'strip'`, `'group'`, `'edge'`, `'float'`, `'dock-guide'`, `'dock-area'` or `'outside'` (refused).": "",
  "The same, just before the drop; cancel keeps everything where it is.": "",
  "Where it ended: `group` is the new group of a split, `document` the copy when one was opened.": "",
  "`{ document, from, dropped, byKeyboard }`, dropped or not.": "",
  "Still fire for what the drop does, so there is one way the model changes. A tab from another manager arrives through `onOpening` there, after `onMoving` here.": "",
  "While dragging: `move`, `copy` or `none` (what a drop would do now); the cursor follows it.": "",
  "The tab, or the group, being dragged.": "",
  "The copy under the pointer; `data-kind` (`tab`, `group`), `data-target` (`move`, `copy`, `none`).": "",
  "The translucent area a drop would take; it glides between places (the motion tokens: none with reduced motion).": "",
  "The mark between two tabs.": "",
  "The group's handle (`groupDragHandle`), a button of the group's toolbar.": "",
  "Their units (the ghost: `copy`, `refused`; a dragged tab: the `tab` unit's `dragging`).": "",
  "The rest of the API is on the [overview](/tabdocs#api), [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs) and [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": ""
}
